TASK/TX V5.52.20 compatibility parameters for the current executable (V5.62 and later).

Merge the namelist lines below into the tx group of a txparm to run the current code with the
default physics of V5.52.20, as far as inputs can bring it back.  They are the defaults that
changed after V5.52.20 (V5.60.00 and later); all other defaults are unchanged.

V5.60.00 (SOL / neutral models):
  FSLP    = 0.3   k_L of the SOL parallel loss        (now 1.0)
  MDLSOL  = 0     historical parallel-loss ramp width (now 1, banana width)
  MDLNZD  = 0     C0-C5 bundle diffused with D01      (now 1, charged bundle + slaved C0)
  MDLWBC  = 0     no density condition at the wall    (now 1, zero gradient)
  MDLN0FL = 0     no Larsen limiter on D01            (same now)
  FLlim and RLXN0 are not used with these settings.
V5.62.00 (momentum pinch, T2):
  PCHRLN  = 1e10  no change of the R/L_n slope        (now 3.8, slope to 0.44 beyond)
  RhoPch1 = 10, RhoPch2 = 11
                  no radial taper of the pinch        (now 1 inside 0.8, 0 outside 0.9)
After V5.62.00 (particle transport, wall, time stepping):
  FSTPTM  = 2     common-velocity closure, model 3    (now 4; 3 from 2026-09-29)
  FSVAHL  = -0.5  thermodiffusion C_T                 (now -0.25)
  PNsSUP  = 0.01, 0.009, 1.6667e-4 with MDLNSUP = 0
                  SOL upstream densities as V5.52 set them once from the default
                  Zeffin = 1.5 (now PNsSUP(1) = 0.026, and with MDLNSUP = 1 PNsSUP(2:3)
                  are derived from PNsSUP(1) and the given Zeffin)
  RWALL = RWALLZ = RWALLIZ = 0
                  no recycling at the main wall       (now 0.98, 0.42, 0)
  NRETRY  = 0     no retry of an unconverged step     (now 1)
  imodel_neo(4) = 0
                  matrix inversion without the potato closure near the axis
                                                      (now 1, orbit-averaged potato)
  EPS     = 1e-3  Picard convergence on the increment (now 1e-5)
  NANDER  = 0     plain Picard sweeps                 (now -20, Anderson acceleration)
  MDLRCY  = 0     target recycling of the SOL loss with its sign
                                                      (now 1, only where it is a net loss)
  MDLNCA  = -1    a step not converged in ICMAX sweeps as V5.52 treated it: accepted with
                  EPS > 0 and MODECV = 0, the run stopped otherwise
                                                      (now 0, by the sign of EPS alone)

Not restored by any input (implementation changes; the results differ slightly):
  - the constant term of the Tala momentum pinch is inward (V5.52: outward, a sign error
    corrected in V5.62), so the pinch is -(mu/R)(1.1 R/L_n + 1), not (mu/R)(1.1 R dlnNe + 1);
  - friction forces assembled with nodal products, conserving momentum discretely (V5.61; O(h^2));
  - V5.61 fast-ion fixes: l_11^fi friction, beam flow variables carrying N_b, no radial beam
    flux at the wall (MDBEAM = 1); they change runs with NBI (core rotation by 0.5-5%);
    with FSRP = 0 the ripple changes do not act;
  - the turbulent force in the wall row in the direct-gradient form, which removed a spurious
    electron inflow at the wall (2026-09-30);
  - the convergence test of psi_t dot with its rounding floor (iteration counts only).
Check (JT-60U-like circular case without NBI, NRMAX = 60, EPS = 1e-6, 1.5 s): with these inputs
the code just before the wall-row fix agrees with V5.52.20 to 2e-4 in n_e and n_i; the current
code is lower by 4.8% in n_e and 8% in n_z, uniformly in radius (the wall-row fix), and agrees to
2% in T_e and 0.5% in T_i.  The current defaults differ by up to 57% in n_e and 94% in n_z.
With NBI (3.2 + 0.4 MW) the densities and temperatures agree to 5-8%, but the core rotation is
40% higher (pinch sign and V5.61 fast-ion fixes).  V5.52.20 itself, run with EPS = 1e-6, stalls
on psi_t dot near the wall; with its default EPS = 1e-3 it does not.
RDltRPn = 2.4 (the former fixed value) is the V5.52 behaviour already.  NANDER is not stored in
the save file, so NANDER = 0 has to stay in the txparm of a run continued from a file.
The save file stores FSTPTM (with FSVAHL and PNsSUP) and imodel_neo, so a run continued from
a file keeps its closures.  It stores MDLRCY since 2026-10-13 (extension record 7): a file
written before takes the MDLRCY of the input, so MDLRCY = 0 has to stay in the txparm of a run
continued from such a file.

 &tx
  FSLP    = 0.3d0
  MDLSOL  = 0
  MDLNZD  = 0
  MDLWBC  = 0
  MDLN0FL = 0
  PCHRLN  = 1.d10
  RhoPch1 = 10.d0
  RhoPch2 = 11.d0
  FSTPTM  = 2.d0, 2.d0, 2.d0
  FSVAHL  = -0.5d0
  MDLNSUP = 0
  PNsSUP  = 0.01d0, 0.009d0, 1.6666666666666666d-4
  RWALL   = 0.d0
  RWALLZ  = 0.d0
  RWALLIZ = 0.d0
  NRETRY  = 0
  imodel_neo(4) = 0
  EPS     = 1.d-3
  NANDER  = 0
  MDLRCY  = 0
  MDLNCA  = -1
 &end
